J.A.R.V.I.S. — NOTIFICATION SYSTEM

1. Purpose

The Notification System allows J.A.R.V.I.S. to communicate important information to the user outside active conversations.

Its purpose is to provide useful reminders, updates and proactive notifications.

2. Notification Types

The system should support:

- Task reminders.
- Scheduled notifications.
- Important alerts.
- Project updates.
- Task completion reports.
- Connection status notifications.
- Assistant status notifications.

3. Reminders

J.A.R.V.I.S. should be able to:

- Create reminders.
- Edit existing reminders.
- Delete reminders.
- Mark reminders as completed.
- Organize reminders by importance.
- Support recurring reminders.

The user should be able to manage all reminders.

4. Proactive Notifications

The assistant may independently suggest notifications when relevant.

Examples:

- An unfinished task.
- An upcoming event.
- An important project deadline.
- A previously requested follow-up.

Proactive notifications should be useful and not excessive.

5. Notification Priority

Notifications should have three priority levels.

Low Priority

General information and optional suggestions.

Normal Priority

Regular reminders and task updates.

High Priority

Important events and time-sensitive information.

The user should be able to customize notification priorities.

6. Notification Settings

The user should be able to:

- Enable or disable notifications.
- Configure notification categories.
- Adjust notification sounds.
- Set quiet hours.
- Control notification frequency.

7. Android Integration

The system should use supported Android notification APIs.

It must respect:

- Notification permissions.
- Background execution restrictions.
- Battery optimization.
- User-defined notification settings.

8. Offline Notifications

Basic scheduled reminders should work without an internet connection whenever Android allows it.

Online-dependent notifications should clearly indicate their requirements.

9. Privacy

Notifications must avoid exposing sensitive information unnecessarily.

The user should be able to control what appears on the lock screen.

10. Future Improvements

Possible future features:

- Context-aware notifications.
- Smart reminder scheduling.
- Priority prediction.
- Voice-based reminders.
- Intelligent notification grouping.

11. Development Status

Status: Planning.

The Notification System has not yet been implemented.
